    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Campus-Security-Specialist_JR50087-1": {
      "title": "Campus Security Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for a Campus Security Specialist to ensure the reliable operation, maintenance and continuous improvement of critical campus security, life-safety and building systems. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile . WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package 13th month Tet bonus for Vietnamese staff Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! Position Summary Property Services team has the responsibility to operate, maintain and enhance the buildings owned by RMIT University, oversee construction projects and ensure the provision of physical facilities services. Property Services consists of the following business units: • Projects • Facilities Management • Campus planning & operations The Campus Security Specialist is responsible for the ongoing health, programming and reliable operation including but not limited to the following systems. •           Electronic Access Control (EAC) •           Closed Circuit Television (CCTV) •           Building Management Systems (BMS) •           Fire Alarm Control System •           Lighting Controls •           Lift Controls •           Emergency Control Room •           Emergency Response System •           Workday for Contract Management of Security related suppliers Working arrangements: The standard working week for this position is Tuesday to Saturday to provide operational coverage over the weekend. The role will also participate in the Emergency Management Team (EMT) 24/7 on-call roster and may be required to respond outside standard working hours, subject to operational requirements. Reporting Line Reports to:  Security Manager Direct reports: Security Supervisor from Security Service Provide & Security admin Reporting lines may be adjusted in line with organisational changes. Key Accountabilities Develop University-wide Security programs, plans, policies, and procedures to ensure safety, and security and reduce the risk for staff, students' contractors, and visitors  Closely lead and manage day-to-day security service provider to ensure the effective management of security operations including emergency and crisis management across 3 campuses. Prioritize the deployment of operational resources across a broad program of work using a risk-based approach  Oversee security needs at all University events and for all University events including performing security risk assessments   Subject matter expert for security develops security solutions for complex University-wide security issues  Identify and improve security vulnerabilities and respond to instances of operational crisis to mitigate further operational legal and reputational issues  Manage stakeholder relationships, including security contractors staff student visitors, and emergency services whilst providing a high level of customer service  Actively evaluate on-campus incidents, recommend and take necessary actions to maintain the security of RMIT's students' administration, faculty, staff, and property Keep track of reported incidents for further review and reporting Create and present incident reports with recommendations for learning from experience and proposing new action plans to avoid repeating events  Lead the investigation of security incidents/complaints including interviews and review of CCTV and provide feedback to students, staff, and customers accordingly  Apply current and new technology to provide technical and operational solutions to senior internal members of staff and work closely with the external contract provider, in relation to day-to-day Security issues to develop a culture of crime prevention incident reduction and traffic management Provide comprehensive reporting on security for senior management including written proposals and reports for action where areas of concern are identified.  Provide forecast analysis and manage Security service budget to ensure high-quality security service with reasonable cost  Develop training plan, materials and provide necessary orientation and training regarding security rules and procedures to contracted security personnel  Collaborate on the development of emergency and continuity plans at various University locations may conduct related training exercises  Undertake any other duties as required by the line manager Key Selection Criteria Bachelor’s in public security or related field At least 5 years of experience in a security related position Sound understanding of legal requirements and standards with regards to public security in Vietnam Significant experience in security management (incl Electronic Security and Surveillance) in a large complex organization including experience in the supervision of large, outsourced security contracts and their related budgets Proven ability to manage day to day operations of a large security team including internal and contracted personnel Extensive experience in successful management of stakeholder relationships within a large complex organization ability to deliver high level of customer service to a wide variety of stakeholders and leadership of a team with a client focused approach to Security services delivery Extensive knowledge of electronic security and surveillance operational systems the security sector regulatory environment and the development and implementation of Security policies and procedures in a large complex organization Excellent written and verbal English and Vietnamese skills, with ability to communicate Ability to write reports and briefs in English9Good judgement and the ability to quickly assess options and make decisions and understanding of risk management in a large complex education organization Proven ability to priorities tasks works to deadlines, manage multiple deliverables work autonomously as well as a productive team member Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position and RMIT Values. HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 12 thg 9 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Hanoi/Expression-of-Interest---Casual-Academic_JR44896": {
      "title": "Expression of Interest – Casual Academic",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam welcome Expressions of Interest (EOI) from talented lecturers and researchers  to join our academic community and deliver high-quality teaching, research, and student engagement. This is an exciting opportunity for an educator-scholar who is passionate about shaping future-ready graduates and contributing to impactful research.  WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM?   At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.  Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the  RMIT Vietnam Profile .  WHAT WE OFFER   Competitive hourly rate.  Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources  A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!  Learn more about Casual ​Academic at RMIT Vietnam. CURRENT VACANCIES IN SEM 3, 2026 We are currently looking for Academic Casual staff to perform specified teaching-related duties, such as presenting lectures and tutorials, conducting practical classes or workshops, and marking with relevant courses/programs in The Business School below: International Business (Global Trade Operations, International Trade and Global Supply Chains, etc.) at SGS Campus Digital Marketing (C onsumer Psychology and Behaviour, Retailing courses) in Hanoi and SGS Campus HRM in Hanoi and SGS Campus Logistics and Supply Chain (Business courses) in Hanoi and SGS Campus Economics ( courses in Digital Economy program) in SGS Campus DISCIPLINES OF INTEREST  We welcome EOIs from candidates with expertise in areas including, but not limited to:  THE BUSSINESS SCHOOL Business Accounting Economics and Finance Human Resource Management Global Business Management Logistics and Supply Chain Management Digital Business Digital Marketing Tourism and Hospitality Management SCHOOL OF DESIGN & COMMUNICATION Professional Communication: Advertising, Digital Communication and Public Relations Digital Media : Interaction design, Animation, Digital imaging, Sound Design Studies: Graphics, Spatial Concepts, Illustration, User Experience Design Game Design : Game Design Studio, Coding Unity, C#  Digital Film and Video : Film-/video-making, Technical studio, Film theory Fashion Enterprise : Design and Product Development, Retail and Merchandising, Customer Relationship Management and Communication SCHOOL OF SCIENCE, ENGINEERING & TECHNOLOGY Engineering: Mechanical, Electrical, Electronics, Robotics, Mechatronics, Manufacturing, Automation  Computing & Technology: Computer Science, Software Engineering, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Cybersecurity  Aviation & Aerospace: Aviation management, aviation safety, airport operations, aerospace systems  Psychology: Clinical psychology, social psychology, Health psychology, Cognitive psychology  KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES SUMMARY    We are currently looking for Academic Casual staff to perform specified teaching-related duties, such as presenting lectures and tutorials, conducting practical classes or workshops, and marking. Casual rates for academic teaching duties include both the presentation or delivery time and the associated working time (including preparation, reasonably contemporaneous marking, and student consultation) and further information can be found in FaQ . ​ Key Selection Criteria   Master's degree (for Associate Lecturer) or PhD degree (for Lecturer )  Minimum 3 years of teaching experience in English-speaking universities in relevant field.  Demonstrated ability to prepare and deliver programs at undergraduate level, including online delivery, and the ability to produce high quality curriculum or program materials.  Industry or professional experience  Culturally adapt and agile     HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible.  COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.  English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn   #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 30 thg 12 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Calling-for-Expression-of-Interest-for-Indigenous-Talent-to-work-in-Academia--VE-and-Professional-roles-at-RMIT--all-campuses-_JR14035": {
      "title": "RMIT invites Aboriginal & Torres Strait Islander peoples to express your interest to work at RMIT (Melbourne, Bundoora or Brunswick campuses) in Professional, Vocational or Academic roles.",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT encourages Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Peoples to apply to be considered for Identified, Targeted, or mainstream roles (Designated EOI)* Explore roles as Teachers, Professional, or Academic staff Possibilities for fixed-term and ongoing roles with flexible hybrid working arrangements Benefit from 17% superannuation, 10 days cultural leave and specialist wellbeing and career support services ​ Why work at RMIT? At RMIT, we celebrate and honour the unique cultures and contributions of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples. We are committed to providing robust support and valuable opportunities during your employment and educational journey, enriched by networking opportunities and the facilities available through our Indigenous Staff Network and the Ngarara Willim Centre. \"The Ngarara Willim Centre is a culturally safe space, advocating for the self-determination and success of our Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students and community through dedicated support and empowerment.\" RMIT is a wonderful place to work in the heart of Melbourne CBD with campuses in Brunswick, Bundoora and Point Cook. We have a thriving and growing Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander community who are making an amazing difference at RMIT though engagement with external Indigenous partners, internal collaborations and training and educating staff on self determination, implementation of Indigenous perspectives, responsible practice and cultural safety. Hear from Professor Gary Thomas, Pro Vice Chancellor for Indigenous Education talk about how RMIT is transitioning through Reconciliation to Responsible Practice https://youtu.be/i5MIrtu3Xew?si=uTkzHyjeguJZlrci What’s on offer? RMIT University is excited to offer new opportunities in 2025-2026 at various levels specifically for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Peoples. We offer attractive salaries, with 17% super and 10 days cultural leave, we also offer hybrid working. See our list of benefits here   Benefits and recognition - RMIT University You could work in the Ngarara Willim Centre dedicated to Indigenous Education or within our Colleges/Portfolios including Vocational Education, STEM, Design, IT, Research or Business and Law. Positions include Identified and Targeted roles, along with mainstream roles. Please submit your EOI application with just a CV and I will be in contact with you following this to discuss possible opportunities at RMIT. You can also browse RMIT's career opportunities here , using \"Indigenous\" as a keyword for identified roles or to have a look at our mainstream roles and apply directly. For further details, contact Loretta Vaughan, Senior Talent Advisor - First Peoples Employment at loretta.vaughan@rmit.edu.au or phone 03 9925 0746 . *Special Measures This is an Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Designated Position, under ‘special measures’ of section 12 of the Equal Employment Opportunity Act 2010. Only Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are eligible to apply to this EOI. We look forward to hearing from you and helping to kickstart your career at RMIT! #LI-Hybrid Applications Close: 30 Dec 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Audio-Visual-Specialist_JR51003": {
      "title": "Audio Visual Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking an Audio Visual Specialist ensures the seamless operation, maintenance, and enhancement of audiovisual technologies across learning and meeting spaces to support teaching, events, and collaboration. The role also leads AV projects, manages vendors and stakeholders, develops user training resources, and recommends innovative solutions to improve the university's AV environment. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile. WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Other benefits Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Audio Visual Specialist will play a crucial role in ensuring the smooth operation and maintenance of audiovisual systems within RMIT Vietnam's classrooms, theaters, and meeting rooms. This role will involve liaising with the Australian team to uphold the university's high standards for AV infrastructure and services. The role will also be responsible for the day-to-day management of AV services, as well as leading and executing projects to fit out new AV spaces and implement innovative initiatives. Key Accountabilities Summary Oversee the operation and maintenance of all audio-visual equipment, including projectors, sound systems, video conferencing systems, and control systems. Monitor the performance of AV systems and troubleshoot technical issues promptly. Work with external vendors on the delivery, implementation and handover of new AV projects and room refresh. Collaborate with the Australian team to understand and implement the university's AV standards and guidelines. Provide recommendations on new AV initiatives and prepare plans and requirements for RMIT Vietnam. Create and maintain AV user educational literacy, such as room operational guides, training demo videos and online FAQ assistance for AV technologies. Liaise with customers and stakeholders requesting AV fit-out services, understand and capture the business needs and operational requirements. Complete regular and ongoing reassessments and analysis of AV and provide input and recommendation for continuous improvement of tools and or processes. Managing AV documentation resources to include room information, schematics, equipment lists, technical and operational manuals, and AV software. Maintain depth of knowledge and understanding of AV industry trends and the range of vendor technologies to meet the AV requirements for the University. Other duties commensurate with the scope of the role Key Selection Criteria A Bachelor degree in relevant field Significant experience within a Technical AV environment working on large scale projects including vendor management. Demonstrated AV installation experience, project management experience desirable. Demonstrated experience in AV technical knowledgebase, AV design, and CAD packages. Demonstrated ability to build effective relationships in a collaborative and engaging manner with a broad range of internal and external stakeholders. Proven ability to work autonomously with minimal supervision. Demonstrated superior analytical and communication skills. Demonstrated ability to prioritise tasks and delivery a quality service to the University. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position and RMIT Values. More information is available in the Job Description . HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 1 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Associate-Registrar_JR50897": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking an  Associate Registrar to join Students and Education Portfolio (SEP) at RMIT Vietnam. The Associate Registrar at RMIT Vietnam plays a pivotal role in advancing the university's objectives and strategies to become a leading institution in Southeast Asia, overseeing crucial responsibilities related to academic records, student enrolment, and regulatory compliance, thereby contributing significantly to the overall success and reputation of the university in the region. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM?   At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.  Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the  RMIT Vietnam Profile .  WHAT WE OFFER Expatriates   Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates  Relocation allowance package from US$6,000  Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate and direct dependents (if applicable)  International repatriation flights for the staff and direct dependents at the end of their contract.  School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to US$20,000 per child or US$40,000 for two children per year.  Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam.   Vietnamese candidates   Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates.  13th month Tet bonus   Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Other benefits   Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays)  Professional development and career advancement  Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources  A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!  THE STUDENTS AND EDUCATION PORTFOLIO The Students and Education Portfolio (SEP) at RMIT Vietnam leads the University’s learning and teaching excellence, curriculum innovation, and integrated student experience. Working in close partnership with academic schools and central portfolios, SEP advances RMIT’s Knowledge with Action strategy and RMIT Vietnam’s Country Commitment by embedding Active, Applied and Authentic (AAA) pedagogies across programs and ensuring students are prepared for future workplaces. SEP brings together academic development, digital innovation, student life, Library and Digital Services, and learning support functions to create an inclusive and engaging learning environment. The portfolio focuses on student success, wellbeing and retention; employability through industry-integrated and work-integrated learning; and the thoughtful integration of digital technologies, including AI, into teaching, assessment and student support. Through this work, SEP plays a central role in positioning RMIT Vietnam as a regional leader in transformative, future-ready education. ABOUT THE ROLE   The Associate Registrar Vietnam, Academic Registrar’s Group (ARG) Vietnam, is responsible for making of key strategic administrative, programming, financial and staffing decisions in relation to student lifecycle and student integrity at RMIT Vietnam. In addition, this position provides inputs in day-to-day operation of ARG in Vietnam and works closely with ARG in Melbourne to support RMIT Vietnam Executive Leadership Team (ELT) in developing seamless approaches to provide an equivalent standard of support and services to students and staff at RMIT Vietnam and to ensure academic policies and processes are best practised. Finally, the position plays a strategic role in large-scale projects such as RMIT scholarships, student system development, and graduation ceremonies to ensure budget, planning, transition, and execution are well in place. It is required that the position works both strategically and operationally across a diverse set of university departments and stakeholders, and to model RMIT values and behaviours in the following five key areas: Government Reporting, Academic Policy planning and Student Visa Compliance. Enrolments and Student Records, including Student Financials Assessment Support, Student Conduct and Complaints Academic Governance and Systems. Completions, Awards and Graduations This position is strategic in nature but retains operational oversight of activities by ARG in RMIT Vietnam  KEY ACCOUNTIBILITIES   To advance the vision of the Students and Education Portfolio (SEP) led by the Dean of Students, collaborate with the relevant leadership teams, develop and implement innovative strategies to ensure alignment with RMIT Vietnam’s regional objectives. To anticipate future trends in higher education and academic administration contributing to the development of RMIT Vietnam and the university as a whole. Working collaboratively with the Academic Registrar’s Group (ARG) leadership team, to own, develop and provide strategic direction in the areas of registry and governance for RMIT Vietnam to succeed with its operational and development goals and objectives. To facilitate functional alignment between RMIT Vietnam and Melbourne operations through respective teams, systems and processes. Identify, highlight, and tabulate proposals to control, prevent, mitigate, and report to higher management critical risks of non-compliance with the academic policies and procedures or scopes of services delivered beyond stipulated regulations or system potential failures. Be an authorised signatory designated by RMIT Vietnam Pro Vice-Chancellor and General Director for student-related documents released to relevant authorities, students or third parties. Be the single point of contact to provide student information and regular reports to statutory authorities following RMIT Privacy Policy and Delegation of Authority Policy. Lead, manage and enhance the delivery of key administrative services across the Student Lifecycle – from the first enrolment to graduation – for preparatory, undergraduate, and post-graduate levels at all RMIT Vietnam locations. Drive the execution of key events including graduation ceremonies and scholarship awards. Ensure governance of assessment support and student conduct processes to protect academic integrity and to best practice Student Conduct Policy and Student Conduct Regulations, facilitating functional alignment between RMIT Vietnam and Australia. Represent the Academic Registrar Group (Vietnam) on relevant working groups and committees, hearing sessions including but not limited to the RMIT Vietnam Incident Management Team (IMT) for matters concerning student complaints, student misconduct, and academic policy. Oversee and provide management support in (i) student-related complaints and (ii) third-party complaints aligning with policies and procedures of the university and in consultation with the ARG Complaint team and the Central Complaints and Investigation team in Australia. Proactive drive and be a conduit for policy review collaborating with RMIT global to provide a voice for RMIT Vietnam, enacting changes, and ensuring relevance to local operations. Be responsible for providing advice and guidance to staff and other stakeholders on academic policies and processes. Pro-actively disseminate changes through different channels including but not limited to training, workshops and communication platforms. Oversee, uplift, and enhance student systems operations and developments being gatekeeper to relevant student and academic platforms to the benefit of RMIT Vietnam. Oversee the development, review and publication of academic calendar, student guides and relevant process documentation; deliver training, workshops, information sessions and presentations for stakeholders and students: ensure information is effectively communicated and published across multiple channels to ensure students and staff are well informed about Student Lifecycle and Student Integrity processes and issues. Create awareness to facilitate functional and governance alignment between RMIT Vietnam and Australia. Liaise, communicate, and collaborate with Academic Schools, Student Connect, Finance and other key departments regularly to support and gather input on the Student Lifecycle and Student Integrity experience. Monitor and provide support on relevant compliance and quality issues and facilitate the resolution of complex issues. For full details of the accountability, please refer to the Job Description . KEY SELECTION CRITERIA A Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field (e.g. business administration, educational leadership, and management). A Master’s degree is desirable as is prior abroad experience. A minimum of 10 years of managerial experience of which at least 5 years of business/operational development experience in an education or training environment, preferably with multinational organisations. Demonstrated leadership and managerial experience in a similar position with excellent administration management and organisational skills, project management and the ability to drive and implement strategic initiatives. A forward-thinker who is one step ahead and has foresight in order to manage issues before they occur. A strong understanding of university policy, governance and processes related to the Student Lifecycle, Student Integrity, and strong operational management skills. Well-versed in Vietnam's local context, government relations and experience in working with local authorities and foreign government agencies, especially in matters related to international students. Demonstrated ability to work with a diverse group of stakeholders with strong presentation and negotiation skills. Track records in developing and implementing relevant policy, processes and protocols across an organisation; demonstrated problem-solving skills and proven experience in managing and providing solutions to complex issues. A data-driven person who embraces changes and improvements in quality management processes to drive continuous improvement. Experience working with databases, customer management systems and relevant software. Excellent communication skills, including written, verbal, and visual communication, experience in writing process documentation and reports, delivering presentations, and the ability to convey complex ideas to diverse audiences. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible.  COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.    English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to Viet Nguyen- Senior Talent Acquisition Advisor at  nguyen.vanviet@rmit.edu.vn    #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 5 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Lecturer--Management_JR46455": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview: We are seeking a Lecturer in Management to join our academic community and deliver high-quality teaching, research, and student engagement. This is an exciting opportunity for an educator-scholar who is passionate about shaping future-ready graduates and contributing to impactful research. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available at Working at RMIT Vietnam . Our benefit: Expatriates   Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates Relocation allowance package of USD $6,000 Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate (and immediate family if applicable). International repatriation flights for the staff, their spouse, and children at the end of their contract. School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to $20,000 per child or $40,000 for two children per year.  Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance. Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam.   Vietnamese candidates   Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates.  13th month bonus.  Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Others Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays). Professional development and career advancement.   Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources. A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!  RMIT Vietnam has been honoured with the respectable HR Asia Award as Top Employer to Work for in Asia. To find out more about RMIT Vietnam and our current vacancies, please visit our website: https://www.rmit.edu.vn/careers . The Business School – A Hub of Innovation, Excellence, and Global Impact   As the largest academic school at RMIT Vietnam, The Business School is home to over 9,000 students across our Ho Chi Minh City and Hanoi campuses. With a diverse and international faculty of more than 160  academic and professional staff from over 15 countries, The Business School offers a dynamic and inclusive environment that fosters excellence in teaching, research, and industry engagement.   Our faculty members are accomplished professionals who have studied, worked and researched in renowned institutions around the world. Their extensive work experience provides our students with valuable industry insights and in-depth knowledge.   We offer a comprehensive suite of programs—from undergraduate to doctoral levels—designed to prepare students for success in an increasingly complex and fast-paced global business environment.  The Business School is proud to be the first in Vietnam to earn  AACSB accreditation, affirming our commitment to world-class standards in business education. Our research strengths span blockchain, cybersecurity, smart cities, and sustainability, contributing to RMIT’s strategic research pillars and shaping the future of business innovation.  As we continue to grow and innovate, we invite passionate professionals to join us in shaping the future of business education in Vietnam and beyond.   More information about The Business School can be found here   Position Summary The Lecturer contributes to Teaching and Research, and Engagement in the Management Program within the Department of Management. The successful candidate will contribute to the development of the program to meet the needs of students and other stakeholders, ensure a consistent level of research is undertaken to support relevant research clusters in the Business School. He/She may deliver courses across related programs as directed. The incumbent also contributes to the strategic direction setting of the program, department, and School by working collaboratively with other relevant members of the department to plan and develop courses, programs, and engagement activities. The successful candidate assists the Senior Program Manager on occasion with administrative decisions and tasks. The scope of responsibilities includes supporting the formulation of strategic planning for the program, course management, where needed, quality assurance, student relationship management, human resource management, program budgeting and resource management and research planning. Key accountabilities Undertake independent teaching at undergraduate, honours and postgraduate level including: designing, conducting and moderating assessment; implementing improvements informed by course evaluation activities and student feedback. Undertake independent professional activities, scholarship and/or conduct high quality research activities appropriate to the profession or discipline including: managing individual projects within timelines and budgets and ensuring compliance with quality and reporting requirements; publishing research results in high quality outlets as lead or co-author; preparing and submitting external research funding applications; and supervising higher degree by research candidates. Undertake administration duties, which may include course coordination role or management of a small award program. Adhere to the requirements of the Academic Expectations and Development Framework of RMIT Vietnam. Our requirements Demonstrated ability to prepare and deliver courses related to Strategy, Leadership, Management, Design Thinking, or Innovation at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including online delivery, and the ability to produce high-quality curriculum or program materials. Ability to undertake course coordination role. Demonstrated capacity to work effectively with and to negotiate sensitively with students especially on issues related to effective learning. Emerging track record and recognition for quality research outputs which will contribute to existing Discipline and School research areas evidenced by publications, development of new research initiatives, competitive research funding, and industry links. Demonstrated ability to supervise higher degree by research candidates. Ability to build effective networks with colleagues and generate alternative funding projects through effective liaison with industry and government. Excellent interpersonal and communications skills appropriate for interacting with higher degree by research candidates, staff and industry, together with a strong commitment to teamwork and multidisciplinary collaboration. Recent and sustained performance regarding student outcomes, student experience and feedback; combined with experience and skill in a range of teaching settings. Ability to operate within own discipline and cross-disciplinary/multidisciplinary teams to achieve department and University strategic outcomes. Ability to work with external partners, industries, organisations and communities and can operate effectively to address complex issues or seek opportunities Ability to motivate, develop and inspire others through discipline leadership in the University environment Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position as per the RMIT Values Expected Research profile   To be considered for a lecturer position at RMIT Vietnam in The Business School, you will need to be able to meet the following research criteria.  For candidates with a PhD awarded within the last 3 years (Early Career Academic), although there are no requirements you are expected to be research active.   For candidates with a PhD awarded within the last 3- 5 years there are requirements of peer reviewed journal articles published within the previous five-year window, you need to be active in relevant research areas.   For candidates with a PhD awarded more than 5 years ago: you will be expected to demonstrate a minimum of 2 peer reviewed journal articles, of which must be ranked in Scimago or ABDC and preferably both in Q1/A ranking or equivalent, within the previous five-year window.  HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible.  COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.    English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application   is submitted through   our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant   about scams asking   for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn   #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 19 thg 9 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/College-of-Business-and-Law---Expression-of-Interest-for-Sessional-Teaching---School-of-Law_JR51143-1": {
      "title": "College of Business and Law - Expression of Interest for Sessional Teaching – School of Law",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nOverview: •    Casual hours commencing February 202 7   •    Based at the Emily McPherson Building located in Melbourne CBD campus but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University or online   About RMIT RMIT offers life-changing experiences for our students, and helps shape the world with research, innovation, teaching and industry engagement. With strong industry connections forged over 130 years, collaboration with industry remains integral to RMIT’s leadership in education, applied and innovative research, and to the development of highly skilled, globally focused graduates.     The College of Business and Law delivers innovative, industry-engaged education and applied research in a global context, supporting RMIT’s Ready for Life and Work strategy through student experience, staff purpose, research impact and global reach.    For further details about the College, please visit: College of Business and Law      School of Law     The School of Law, established in 2025 , evolved from the former Graduate School of Business and Law. Situated in the historic Emily McPherson Building, it offers RMIT law students an engaging and dynamic learning environment, enriched by state-of-the-art resources, experienced teaching staff, and strong industry connections.     As one of four schools within RMIT’s College of Business and Law, the School delivers the Bachelor of Laws (including double degrees) and the Juris Doctor program, both accredited by the Victorian Legal Admissions Board.     Committed to excellence in teaching and research, the School prepares students for the demands of the legal profession and beyond. Its curriculum covers all core law subjects, complemented by a wide range of electives and practical skills development, including advocacy, interviewing, and negotiation simulations. The School also fosters a collegial and supportive community that encourages both academic and professional growth.     Further information regarding RMIT’s School of Law and our programs can be found here.   Express Your Interest    We welcome expressions of interest from both external applicants and current RMIT casual employees interested in contributing to the School of Law programs.      To submit your expression of interest, please click ‘Apply’ and submit a current CV and covering letter addressing the following: 1- Please outline what type of work you would be interested in:    • Teaching    • Marking    • Online Teachin g (available only for sessional teachers based in Victoria)   2- Please briefly outline your academic and/or professional experience .   3- If you are interested in tutoring or teaching, please provide a summary of your teaching ability and your capacity to engage students positively and constructively .   4- If you would like to be considered for future casual research opportunities, please briefly outline your research interest .   Please note: The volume, nature and availability of sessional teaching will vary based on the needs of the school including course offerings, timetabling and student demand.     Although our needs and vacancies regularly change , there are opportunities that exist across our programs. By submitting an application, you will be included into a Talent Pool that will be reviewed across the year and may not guarantee a position.      Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children Check.   For further information about this position, please contact casualrecruitment@rmit.edu.au via email.     Applications Close: 17 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Casual-VE-Teacher---Mechanical--Aerospace---Civil-Engineering_JR51167": {
      "title": "Casual VE Teacher,  Mechanical, Aerospace & Civil Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nOverview: Casual hours  commencing ASAP   Teaching into Advanced Diploma of Engineering Technology (Civil Engineering Design) Based at the Melbourne City Campus   About You    As a Casual Teacher within RMIT’s College of Vocational Education, you will be mainly responsible for the delivery of course material, assessing students and the supervision of students enrolled in selected courses within the program.      You will participate in the program’s continuing review of course content and development, delivery, teaching methods (including online delivery methods) and methods of students’ assessment.   Your performance will be underpinned by participation in relevant activities which ensure your vocational competence meets and/or exceeds the education level being delivered and assessed.     We are looking for VE Teachers to assist in the program of Advanced Diploma of Engineering Technology (Civil Engineering Design). To be successful in this position, you’ll have as a minimum:     Qualification in Engineering (Civil Engineering Design)   Industry experience in Engineering   A valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check    Certificate IV in Training and Assessment (TAE40110 or higher)  is required About the College     The purpose of RMIT’s College of Vocational Education is to empower learners and our industry, community and government partners to succeed in the new world of work.     Our five-year strategic roadmap, ALiVE@RMIT, purposefully guides everything we do in vocational education to deliver our vision: to position RMIT as a leading multi-sector provider with global impact and influence.     Led by our Pro Vice Chancellor, the College of VE is reimagining how we deliver vocational education to create unique experiences for our students and partners, so we can:   •    lead in practice-based learning   •    empower learners for the future of work   •    engage industry and community at scale   •    grow for impact and influence     The College of VE is delivering impact through transformation that creates long-term change.   To  Apply     Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘Apply’ link at the top of this page.      For further information about this position, please contact Mykayla McCartin via Mykayla.mccartin@rmit.edu.au    Applications Close: 18 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Lecturer--International-Business_JR48414": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer, International Business",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in International Business to join our academic community in Ho Chi Minh City or Hanoi . In this role, you will deliver high-quality teaching, contribute to impactful research, and engage meaningfully with students. Applicants with teaching and research expertise in Global Business, Global Corporate Responsibility, Cross‑Cultural Management, Global Trade Operations, Political Economy of Global Business , or other closely related areas of International Business are strongly encouraged to apply WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM?   At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.  Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the  RMIT Vietnam Profile .  WHAT WE OFFER   Expatriates   Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates  Relocation allowance package from US$6,000  Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate and direct dependents (if applicable)  International repatriation flights for the staff and direct dependents at the end of their contract.  School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to US$20,000 per child or US$40,000 for two children per year.  Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam.   Vietnamese candidates   Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates.  13th month Tet bonus   Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Other benefits   Generous annual leave, career leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays)  Professional development and career advancement  Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources  A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!  POSITION SUMMARY   Lecturer/Senior Lecturer contributes to Teaching and Research, and Engagement in the International Business Program within the Department of Management. The successful candidate will contribute to the development of the program to meet the needs of students and other stakeholders, ensure a consistent level of research is undertaken to support relevant research clusters in the Business School. He/She may deliver courses across related programs as directed. The incumbent also contributes to the strategic direction setting of the program, department, and School by working collaboratively with other relevant members of the department to plan and develop courses, programs, and engagement activities. The successful candidate assists the Senior Program Manager on occasion with administrative decisions and tasks. Key Accountabilities summary    Undertake independent teaching at undergraduate, honours and postgraduate level, including designing, conducting, and moderating assessment; implementing improvements informed by course evaluation activities and student feedback Undertake independent professional activities, scholarship and/or conduct high quality research activities appropriate to the profession or discipline including: managing individual projects within timelines and budgets and ensuring compliance with quality and reporting requirements; publishing research results in high quality journals as lead or co-author; preparing and submitting external research funding applications; and supervising HDR candidates Contribute to the development of a research-based culture within the program through individual and collaborative research activities Manage course amendment processes and course-related policies, pursuant to the School, College and University procedures and in liaison with RMIT Melbourne Key Selection Criteria   PhD or equivalent Doctoral qualification in International Business or closely related areas Experience in preparing and delivering undergraduate and postgraduate programs in the following courses: Global Business, Global Corporate Responsibility, Cross Cultural Management, Global Trade Operations, and Political Economy of Global Business . This includes online delivery and the creation of high-quality curriculum materials. Ability to coordinate and develop courses. Proven ability to work effectively with students, particularly on learning-related issues. Established track record in quality research outputs contributing to program and School research areas. Experience in supervising higher degree research candidates. Proven ability to generate alternative funding projects through effective networking with colleagues, industry, and government. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with a commitment to teamwork and multidisciplinary collaboration. Proven performance in student outcomes and experience, with skills in various teaching settings Expected Research profile   To be considered for a lecturer position at RMIT Vietnam in The Business School, you will need to be able to meet the following research criteria.  For candidates with a PhD awarded within the last 3 years (Early Career Academic), although there are no requirements you are expected to be research active.   For candidates with a PhD awarded within the last 3- 5 years there are requirements of peer reviewed journal articles published within the previous five-year window, you need to be active in relevant research areas.   For candidates with a PhD awarded more than 5 years ago: you will be expected to demonstrate a minimum of 2 peer reviewed journal articles, of which must be ranked in Scimago or ABDC and preferably both in Q1/A ranking or equivalent, within the previous five-year window.  To be considered for a Senior Lecturer position and above, The Business School operates a research active points system. Points are earned across a spectrum of research within a prior three-year window. Candidates for higher level positions will be considered against these criteria for shortlisting.  More information is available in the Job Description      HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be conducting a rolling recruitment process. Applications will be reviewed and progressed as they are received. Early submission is encouraged, as the University reserves the right to make an appointment prior to the advertised closing date. COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.    English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn   #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 18 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Lecturer--Senior-Lecturer---Digital-Marketing_JR48193": {
      "title": "Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer - Digital Marketing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Digital Marketing to contribute to teaching, research, and engagement within the Digital Marketing program in the Department of Business Innovation. We welcome applications from candidates with teaching and research expertise in areas including, but not limited to Digital Marketing Strategy and Planning, Digital Marketing Communications, Social Media and Mobile Marketing, and Contemporary Issues in Digital Marketing. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM?   At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.  Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the  RMIT Vietnam Profile .  WHAT WE OFFER   Expatriates   Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates  Relocation allowance package from US$6,000  Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate and direct dependents (if applicable)  International repatriation flights for the staff and direct dependents at the end of their contract.  School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to US$20,000 per child or US$40,000 for two children per year.  Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam.   Vietnamese candidates   Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates.  13th month Tet bonus   Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Other benefits   Generous annual leave, career leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays)  Professional development and career advancement  Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources  A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!  POSITION SUMMARY   The Lecturer/Senior Lecturer contributes to Teaching and Research, and Engagement in the Digital Marketing Program within the Department of Business Innovation. The successful candidate will contribute to the development and delivery of undergraduate and postgraduate courses and programs to meet the needs of students and other stakeholders, ensure a consistent level of research is undertaken to support relevant research clusters in the Business School, and work collaboratively with other academic staff to support a strong research culture within the Digital Marketing team. The successful candidate may deliver courses across related programs as directed. The incumbent also contributes to the strategic direction-setting of the program, department, and School by working collaboratively with other relevant members of the department to plan and develop courses, programs, and engagement activities. This includes contributing to the design, development, amendment and continuous improvement of undergraduate and postgraduate courses, the development of new courses at both levels, and the initiation of teaching and learning initiatives relevant to Digital Marketing and related programs. The successful candidate assists the Senior Program Manager on occasion with administrative decisions and tasks. The scope of responsibilities includes supporting the formulation of strategic planning for the program, course management, where needed, quality assurance, student relationship management, human resource management, program budgeting and resource management and research planning. The Lecturer/Senior Lecturer will act in accordance with the Academic Expectations framework of RMIT University Vietnam. Key Selection Criteria   PhD or equivalent relevant Doctoral qualification Demonstrated ability to prepare and deliver programs at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including online delivery, and the ability to produce high-quality curriculum or program materials. Ability to undertake course coordination and development roles. Demonstrated capacity to work effectively with and to negotiate sensitively with students especially on issues related to effective learning. Established track record and recognition for quality research outputs which will contribute to existing program and School research areas evidenced by publications, development of new research initiatives, competitive research funding, and industry links. Demonstrated ability to supervise higher degree by research candidates. Ability to build effective networks with colleagues and generate alternative funding projects through effective liaison with industry and government. Excellent interpersonal and communications skills appropriate for interacting with higher degree by research candidates, staff and industry, together with a strong commitment to teamwork and multidisciplinary collaboration. Recent and sustained performance regarding student outcomes, student experience and feedback; combined with experience and skill in a range of teaching settings. Ability to operate within own discipline and cross-disciplinary/multidisciplinary teams to achieve department and University strategic outcomes. Ability to work effectively with external partners, industry, organisations and communities to address complex issues and identify opportunities. Ability to motivate, develop and inspire others through discipline leadership in the University environment. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model (Inclusion, Imagination, Agility, Courage, Passion and Impact). Expected Research profile   To be considered for a lecturer position at RMIT Vietnam in The Business School, you will need to be able to meet the following research criteria.  For candidates with a PhD awarded within the last 3 years (Early Career Academic), although there are no requirements you are expected to be research active.   For candidates with a PhD awarded within the last 3- 5 years there are requirements of peer reviewed journal articles published within the previous five-year window, you need to be active in relevant research areas.   For candidates with a PhD awarded more than 5 years ago: you will be expected to demonstrate a minimum of 2 peer reviewed journal articles, of which must be ranked in Scimago or ABDC and preferably both in Q1/A ranking or equivalent, within the previous five-year window.  To be considered for a Senior Lecturer position and above, The Business School operates a research active points system. Points are earned across a spectrum of research within a prior three-year window. Candidates for higher level positions will be considered against these criteria for shortlisting.  More information is available in the Job description    HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be conducting a rolling recruitment process. Applications will be reviewed and progressed as they are received. Early submission is encouraged, as the University reserves the right to make an appointment prior to the advertised closing date. COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.    English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn   #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 18 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Lecturer_JR50855": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Signal Processing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Continuing position Salary Academic Level B ($119,915 - $142,402 p.a.) + 17% Superannuation and Flexible Working Arrangements Primarily based at Melbourne City campus, and the potential to work across other RMIT campuses as required. About the Role Join RMIT’s School of Engineering as a Lecturer in Signal Processing and help shape the next generation of biomedical engineers. This continuing Level B role offers the opportunity to combine high-quality teaching with research in biomedical signal processing, machine learning and related areas, while contributing to an inclusive, industry-connected academic environment. You will teach across undergraduate, Masters and Graduate Diploma programs, develop contemporary curriculum, support student learning, and build partnerships with academic, industry and professional communities. You will work collaboratively with colleagues in Biomedical Engineering and may also contribute to course coordination, research supervision and initiatives that strengthen RMIT’s impact in health, technology and engineering. Why work with us? This is an opportunity for an emerging academic to grow their teaching, research and industry engagement profile in a university known for applied, work-connected learning and research with real-world impact. You will be part of a supportive STEM College community that values collaboration, accountability, respect and empowerment, with access to multidisciplinary networks across engineering, health innovation, digital technologies and industry partnerships.   To be successful in this position, you’ll have: Demonstrated track record in biomedical signal processing and machine learning Demonstrated ability to design, prepare and deliver programs at undergraduate and post-graduate levels (including online and blended delivery), and the ability to produce high-quality curriculum or program materials using inclusive learning and teaching approaches Ability to undertake course coordination role and embedding technology-enhanced course design and delivery. Demonstrated capacity to work effectively with and to negotiate sensitively with students especially on issues related to effective learning. Emerging track record and recognition for quality research outputs which will contribute to existing Discipline and School research areas evidenced by publications, development of new research initiatives, competitive research funding, and industry links. Demonstrated ability to supervise higher degree by research candidates. Ability to build effective networks with colleagues and generate alternative funding projects through effective liaison with industry and government, particularly in biomedical engineering sector. Excellent interpersonal and communications skills appropriate for interacting with higher degree by research candidates, staff and industry, together with a strong commitment to teamwork and multidisciplinary collaboration and inclusive practices.   Qualifications: Mandatory: PhD or equivalent  in relevant field. Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check. About the STEM College LEARN! GROW! DO! Together transforming the world through STEM STEM College is a community of exceptional researchers, teachers, inventors, designers and game changers, supported by talented professional staff. We deliver higher education programs across STEM disciplines at Bachelor, Master and PhD levels, with a strong focus on work-aligned, life-changing student experiences. Our research strengths span advanced manufacturing and design, computing technologies, health innovation and translational medicine, nano materials and devices, and sustainable systems. Industry is central to what we do, helping ensure our research creates real-world impact and our students graduate ready to contribute. We are proud of our inclusive and caring culture, and we support every member of our community to achieve their potential. In STEM we CARE – Collaboration, Accountability, Respect and Empowerment. For further information about the STEM College please visit the following site:  https://www.rmit.edu.au/about/schools-colleges/stem-college To Apply  Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing the Key Selection Criteria for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page. For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Professor Kate Fox via email kate.fox@rmt.edu.au For further information regarding recruitment processes, please contact Jennifer Pham, Senior Talent Acquisition Advisor via email at jennifer.pham2@rmit.edu.au Please do not share your application to this email address.       Position Description – Lecturer, Signal Processing Applications Close: 29 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Academic--Level-C-E--in-Communication-Network-Engineering_JR50820-2": {
      "title": "Academic (Level C-E) in Communication/Network Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Continuing position Salary Academic Level C ($146,897 - $169,387 p.a.), Level D ($176,883 - $194,868 p.a.) or Level E ($227,847 p.a.) + 17% Superannuation Based at the Melbourne CBD campus but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University   Teaching commitments can include offshore fly-in fly-out (FIFO) delivery.   About the Role RMIT University is seeking to appoint an outstanding academic in Communication/Network Engineering within the Department of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, School of Engineering. This is one continuing, full-time position that may be appointed at Academic Level C, D or E, depending on the successful candidate’s experience, track record and level of appointment sought. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching, research, industry engagement and academic leadership in areas including communication engineering, network engineering, network security, telecommunications infrastructure, wireless and space communications, 6G and beyond, and advanced communication and networking technologies. We are particularly interested in candidates with strong theoretical foundations and hands-on expertise in the design, development, integration and validation of telecommunications systems, including capability in areas such as software-defined radios, RFSoCs, RF and millimetre-wave systems and devices, high-speed signal processing, embedded system design, network simulators and emulators, network security simulators, and network testbeds such as ORAN. The appointment level will be determined with reference to the candidate’s demonstrated academic achievements, research profile, teaching capability, leadership experience and alignment with the relevant Academic Level C, D or E expectations. To be considered for appointment at Level C, you will have: An emerging nationally recognised research track record in communication engineering, networks and security, 6G and beyond, aerial and space communications, including substantial research outputs in high-quality outlets. Experience in the design and development of research testbeds, integrating hardware platforms and associated software systems to test, validate, and evaluate research outcomes in practical environments. Demonstrated ability to coordinate large courses and deliver high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, including curriculum development, assessment design and student-centred learning improvements. Experience developing and leading high-quality research projects, attracting external research funding, supervising higher degree by research candidates, and building productive research collaborations. To be considered for appointment at Level D, you will also have: A nationally recognised research track record with a substantial record of research outputs in high-quality outlets and emerging international recognition. Advanced knowledge and experience in the design and development of research testbeds, integrating hardware platforms and associated software systems to test and validate research outcomes, evaluate system performance, and demonstrate engineering concepts in practical and realistic operating environments. Extensive research leadership experience, including the ability to build and mentor collaborative research teams, attract and manage external research funding, and deliver high-quality outcomes. Demonstrated ability to lead advancement in teaching, implement program improvements, contribute to academic governance, and support scholarly development within the discipline. To be considered for appointment at Level E, you will also have: A distinguished national and internationally recognised research profile, with evidence of eminent standing and sustained contribution to the discipline. Extensive knowledge and experience in the design, development, and deployment of research testbeds, integrating hardware and software systems to test and validate research outcomes, demonstrate concepts in practical environments, and advance proposed solutions towards higher Technology Readiness Levels (TRLs). Proven ability to establish, sustain and grow research groups, centres or major research programs through external funding, partnerships and high-impact research outputs. Demonstrated strategic academic leadership, including leading teaching and research excellence, contributing to School, College and University strategy, and influencing the wider professional, industry or community sector. Qualifications: Mandatory for appointment at Level C, D or E: PhD in a related field or approved AQF equivalency with relevant industry experience.   Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.   Department of Electrical & Electronic Engineering The Department of Electrical & Electronic Engineering is one of RMIT’s largest departments, with a strong reputation for research and innovation across photonics, electrification, sensors, electronic manufacturing, power and automation/control, and telecommunication systems and networks. In 2025, the department's research grant income exceeded $17 million, with nearly $65 million secured over the past five years.   The Department leads major research initiatives including COMBS, the D2D manufacturing facility, COMAS and the national centre for electrification, and has strong engagement with defence and industry partners in RF systems, antennas, materials, space and wireless communications. The Department delivers undergraduate and postgraduate programs across electrical, power, control and automation; analog/digital, RF and microelectronics; embedded, computer and software; and communication and networks. The Department also delivers offshore teaching programs in Hong Kong and India and maintains strong industry partnerships across funded research, work-integrated learning, student placements and project co-supervision. To Apply  Submit your CV, cover letter, and a separate document addressing the Key Selection Criteria via the ‘Apply’ link below. In your cover letter, state the academic level you wish to be considered for: Level C, Level D or Level E. If you are open to more than one level, please indicate this clearly. For further information about this position, please see the Position Descriptions hyperlinked below or contact Professor Kandeepan Sithamparanathan via email kandeepan.sithamparanathan@rmit.edu.au   For further information regarding recruitment processes, please contact Jennifer Pham, Senior Talent Acquisition Advisor via email at jennifer.pham2@rmit.edu.au Please do not share your application to this email address.       Position Description – Senior Lecturer (Level C) Position Description – Associate Professor (Level D) Position Description – Professor (Level E) Applications Close: 26 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Head-of-Strategy---Operations_JR51285": {
      "title": "Head of Strategy & Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Continuing position 10C + 17% Superannuation and Flexible Working Arrangements Key strategic leadership role based at the Melbourne CBD campus   About the role   The Head of Strategy and Operations, Office of the Vice-President Engagement is a senior leadership role providing strategic and operational leadership to the Office and supporting the effective performance of the broader Engagement Portfolio.   Reporting directly to the Vice-President Engagement, you will act as a trusted strategic adviser and thought leader, providing high-level advice, anticipating emerging issues and opportunities, managing risk and helping shape and advance key Portfolio priorities.   You will lead complex strategic initiatives, cross-functional programs and priority projects, working with senior stakeholders across the University to drive alignment, collaboration and organisational outcomes. Leading a small team, you will also foster a high-performing, collaborative and service-oriented culture, while strengthening governance, systems, operating rhythms and ways of working to support effective decision-making and delivery.   Key Responsibilities   Act as the principal strategic adviser/chief of staff to the Vice-President Engagement, providing high-level advice and insights to support effective decision-making and University priorities. Lead complex strategic projects and cross-functional initiatives, managing risks, dependencies, budgets and delivery outcomes. Lead the Office of the Vice-President Engagement, fostering a high-performing, collaborative and service-focused culture. Contribute to the Portfolio Senior Leadership Team, supporting effective coordination and operations across the Portfolio. Oversee Portfolio planning, governance, performance, risk and reporting, ensuring alignment with strategic priorities. Drive operational efficiency and continuous improvement, including effective business processes, issue resolution and prioritisation. Support financial and resource management, including planning, budget oversight, monitoring and reporting.   To be successful in this position, you’ll have:   Prior tertiary engagement experience including alumni, philanthropy, industry engagement, marketing, communications and student recruitment, in support of the institution’s teaching, learning, research and engagement objectives. Strong experience either as a Chief of Staff or Senior Principle trusted advisor role, offering strategy development and executive support within a complex tertiary education institution. Proven leadership and stakeholder management, with the ability to build high-performing teams, influence outcomes and foster strong relationships. Demonstrated ability to lead complex strategic initiatives, manage competing priorities and deliver outcomes in fast-changing environments. Strong capability across governance, risk, strategic planning, problem-solving and executive communication Relevant post-graduate degree in public policy, MBA or equivalent qualifications and/or demonstrated experience  Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.   About the Portfolio   The Engagement Portfolio actively partners with RMIT's diverse communities to co-create value.  We protect and enhance RMIT’s global reputation, reach and revenue, working collaboratively across Colleges and other Portfolios to deliver the University’s mission and strategic priorities.​   We bring together key functions including current student and staff communications, global marketing, digital experience, global student recruitment, market insights, philanthropy, alumni and industry engagement.    To Apply  Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing the Key Selection Criteria for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.   For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Bianca Jenkins via email bianca.jenkins@rmit.edu.au.    PD Description   Please note, if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, position description links may not work on LinkedIn advertisements.     #LI-Hybrid Applications Close: 18 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/VE-Teacher---VE-Teacher--Engineering--Electrical---Telecoms_JR50780": {
      "title": "VE Teacher - Engineering, Electrical & Telecoms",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Continuing position   Salary teacher level T3.1 to T5 + 17% Superannuation   Based at the Melbourne CBD campuses however, but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University   Great benefits such as 17% Super, 720 teaching hours per year, 4 weeks leave + 2 weeks VE Leave, Strong Industry Connections, Value-Led and Inclusive Environment, generous annual, personal and parental leave, Employee Assistance Program, Medical Hub on Campus, Novated Car Leasing, 25% discount on some short courses, personal software discounts, among others     About the position   The VE Teacher – Engineering, Electrical & Telecoms is responsible for delivering high-quality vocational education and training within the engineering discipline at RMIT University. The role focuses on providing industry-relevant teaching and assessment in Electrical Engineering and Telecommunications, supporting students to develop practical skills, technical capability, and professional readiness for the engineering sector.  The successful candidate will be an Engineering professional with qualifications in Engineering or a related field, with preference given to candidates holding a Master’s or PhD qualification. Candidates will demonstrate teaching experience within Higher Education (HE) and/or Vocational Education (VE) environments, with the ability to deliver engaging, student-centred learning experiences.  The position requires the delivery of associate degree in engineering technology and competency-based training and assessment aligned with vocational education standards, including curriculum development, student support, and continuous improvement activities. A Certificate IV in Training and Assessment (TAE40116 or equivalent) is essential for this role. A proof of enrolment is required if Certificate IV in Training and Assessment (TAE40116 or equivalent) is not yet awarded.  The VE Teacher will work collaboratively with academic teams and industry stakeholders to ensure programs remain contemporary, practical, and aligned with industry expectations, contributing to RMIT’s commitment to excellence in applied and vocational education.    To be successful in this position, you’ll have:   Demonstrated skills and experience in grading and competency-based assessment.  Ability in ensuring current and contemporary vocational competence which meets and/or exceeds the education level being delivered and assessed.  Experience in relevant industry, and substantial discipline knowledge as it relates to this position.  Capacity to diagnose learning problems in students, propose and implement effective solutions.  Demonstrated skills in the use of relevant information and communication technologies.  Qualifications   Certificate 4 Training & Assessment (TAE40110 or higher)   Master or PhD in Engineering (preferably)    Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.     To Apply    Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing the Key selection criteria by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.  For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Mykayla via mykayla.mccartin@rmit.edu.au    Position Description -  VE Teacher: Engineering, Electrical & Telecoms #LI-Hybrid  Applications Close: 31 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/First-Nations-Research-Communications-Officer--Identified-_JR50773": {
      "title": "First Nations Research Communications Officer (Identified)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nOverview: Identified role for Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander candidates Full time, fixed-term position supporting First Nations digital inclusion research Hew 5 ($84,181p.a plus 17% superannuation and cultural leave) Flexible working arrangements, including hybrid working Based at RMIT City campus with some optional travel to research and field sites About the role RMIT University is seeking a creative and self-motivated Research Communications and Engagement Officer to help translate important research into accessible, engaging and culturally respectful communications. Working as part of the research team, you will contribute to the Measuring Digital Inclusion and Mapping the Digital Gap project. This work explores digital inclusion and the digital experiences of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples and communities, helping to communicate research findings in ways that are meaningful, accessible and useful to a range of audiences. Research translation is central to this role. You will turn research insights, data and project activities into clear and engaging content for digital platforms, reports, social media and stakeholder communications. Graphic design is a key part of the position, including creating social media content, reports, promotional materials and data visualisations. You will also help grow and improve the project’s social media presence, particularly across social media platforms , and support the maintenance and development of related digital content and web pages. The role will involve working closely with researchers and the wider ADM+S Centre operations team on project communications, engagement, web content and events. This is a largely self-managed position suited to someone who can work independently, take initiative and manage competing priorities without requiring close supervision. We are looking for someone with relevant communications, engagement or graphic design experiencenwho is passionate about communicating research and creating positive change for First Nations communities. About the project The role will contribute to research focused on measuring digital inclusion and mapping the digital gap, including the Mapping the Digital Gap and First Nations Digital Inclusion projects. For further information, please visit: Mapping the Digital Gap First Nations Digital Inclusion Mapping the Digital Gap on Facebook Key selection criteria Must be of Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander heritage as an essential selection criterion. Demonstrated understanding of the issues affecting Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander people Demonstrated high level ability to communicate sensitively and effectively with Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples Experience or training in communications, graphic design, public relations, engagement or a related field. Demonstrated experience in graphic design, particularly for digital communications, reports, publications or social media. Experience translating complex information, research or data into clear, engaging and accessible content for different audiences. Experience creating and improving social media content, particularly for Facebook and LinkedIn. The ability to develop digital graphics, reports and data visualisations. Familiarity with Adobe Creative Cloud products, particularly InDesign, Illustrator and Photoshop, and with Canva. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to communicate respectfully and effectively with diverse audiences. Ability to work independently, manage your own workload, take initiative and meet deadlines with limited supervision. Ability to work collaboratively with researchers, project partners and the wider operations team. A commitment to culturally respectful and inclusive practice and to communicating research in ways that benefit Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples and communities. Desirable experience Working in an academic, research or community environment. Managing web content, including basic HTML, CSS or SEO Experience with social media reporting, analytics or digital engagement metrics. Experience using data visualisation tools or presenting research findings visually. Photography, filming or basic audio-visual equipment. Experience using Adobe Premiere Pro or After Effects. Qualifications A relevant bachelor’s degree with subsequent relevant experience in communications, public relations and/or engagement, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience, education or training, is required. Position Description Identified position This is an Identified position and being an Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person is considered a genuine occupational qualification in accordance with sections 26(3) and 28 of the Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic). The successful applicant will be required to provide confirmation of their Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander heritage. RMIT is committed to creating a culturally safe, supportive and inclusive environment for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff and students. We warmly encourage applications from people who bring lived experience, cultural knowledge, community connections and a passion for sharing First Nations research and stories in respectful ways. Appointment to this position is subject to holding a valid Victorian Working with Children Check and other checks as required for the specific role. Maintaining a valid Working with Children Check is a condition of employment at RMIT. Applications close 11:59 pm Sunday 18 October 2026 To apply Please submit your CV and a covering letter addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the Apply link. For further information if required, please contact loretta.vaughan@rmit.edu.au - do not send your application here. Applications Close: 27 Sept 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Social-Media---Community-Specialist_JR51290": {
      "title": "Social Media & Community Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for a creative, strategic and social-savvy Social Media & Community Specialist to shape how our brand shows up online, grow and engage our communities, and create content that connects with prospective students and parents across Facebook, TikTok, Instagram, Threads and emerging platforms.   In line with our current recruitment and selection guidelines, this role is open to Vietnamese candidates only. Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity.   Portfolio requirement: Candidates should submit a portfolio demonstrating social media strategy, content planning, channel growth/community engagement and social content, clearly outlining their role and outcomes for selected examples.   WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.   Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile .   WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for candidates. 13th month bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!   POSITION SUMMARY The Social Media & Community Specialist is responsible for developing and leading RMIT Vietnam’s social media strategy and audience growth across platforms including Facebook, TikTok, Instagram, Threads and emerging social channels.   The role leads the development of engaging, audience-relevant content and social experiences that build brand love, brand consideration and meaningful relationships with prospective students and parents. The role uses audience insights, social listening, platform trends and performance data to shape channel strategy, content direction and continuous optimisation. You will also build and manage a network of content contributors, providing direction, coaching and governance to ensure a consistent, high-quality RMIT social presence. The role works closely with Marketing, Schools and other internal stakeholders to identify opportunities to strengthen RMIT’s presence and relevance in social conversations, while ensuring all activity is aligned with the RMIT brand and broader marketing objectives.   Key Accountabilities summary Social media strategy & channel growth Develop and execute RMIT Vietnam’s social media strategy across Facebook, TikTok, Instagram, Threads and emerging platforms, with a focus on brand love, consideration, audience growth and engagement. Define channel priorities, content pillars and growth opportunities based on audience insights, trends and performance data. Social content planning & creation Lead and develop social content plan, build content direction and initiate ideas for social channels Execute the aligned content plan, producing content from written to video formats Ensure content is relevant to priority audiences and aligned with RMIT’s brand, campaigns and broader marketing objectives. Community engagement & social listening Build meaningful relationships with prospective students and parents through proactive community engagement and social conversations. Monitor and generate social conversations, evaluate audience sentiment and emerging trends to identify brand opportunities and manage potential issues. Performance & optimisation Monitor channel and content performance, audience behaviour and competitor activity, translating insights into recommendations to improve reach, engagement and channel growth. Test new formats, creative approaches and platform opportunities to continuously optimise performance. Contributor network & collaboration Build and coordinate a network of social content contributors, providing guidance, feedback and quality standards to enable authentic and diverse social content. Collaborate with academic Schools and other stakeholders to identify stories and opportunities for social. Key Selection Criteria 4+ years' experience in social media, digital content or a related field, with demonstrated experience developing and executing social media strategies across multiple platforms. Strong experience in social channel strategy, audience growth, community engagement and platform-specific content, particularly Facebook, TikTok, and emerging platforms. Strong creative storytelling through copywriting and short-form video content creation, with a portfolio demonstrating high-quality social content and successful campaigns or channel initiatives. Demonstrated ability to use social media analytics, audience insights and trends to optimise content and channel performance. Experience coordinating, coaching or managing content contributors, creators, agencies or cross-functional teams. Strong stakeholder management, communication, organisation and prioritisation skills, with the ability to manage multiple channels and priorities in a fast-paced environment. Appointment to this position is subject to passing mandatory check. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model.   For full details of the accountability, please refer to the Job Description.   HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the University reserves the right to appoint prior to the closing date.   Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.  English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).  Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.   RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.   IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at nhu.tranngocquynh@rmit.edu.vn Applications Close: 1 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Assistant-Manager--Tax-Governance---Technology_JR51085": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Tax Governance & Technology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for an Assistant Manager, Tax Governance and Technology to support key tax compliance, governance and technology workstreams. The role will work closely with Finance teams and stakeholders to strengthen tax processes, data quality, controls and audit readiness in line with Vietnamese tax regulations and RMIT policies. Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Assistant Manager, Tax Governance and Technology manages key tax compliance, documentation, review and tax technology workstreams that support the effective operation of RMIT Vietnam’s tax function. The role reviews and analyses tax information, coordinates with Finance teams, internal stakeholders, external advisors and other relevant parties, and contributes to the accurate and timely delivery of tax obligations. It also contributes to tax governance, audit readiness, tax data quality, data automation, reconciliation, visualisation and continuous improvement of tax processes, controls, systems and documentation practices in accordance with Vietnamese tax regulations and RMIT policies. Reporting Line  Reports to:  Senior Manager, Reporting and Tax Direct Reports: Associate Director, Finance Reporting lines may be adjusted in line with organisational changes. Key Accountabilities Summary 1. Tax compliance, documentation and review Manage key tax compliance workstreams, including preparation and review of tax calculations, reconciliations, working papers and related tax reporting inputs for applicable tax obligations. Maintain and review tax records, supporting documentation, working papers and tax schedules to support tax filing, internal review, external audit, tax health check and tax authority inspection. Coordinate month-end and year-end tax-related processes, including tax reporting inputs, tax reconciliations, tax provisions and tax-related accounting matters. Ensure confidentiality, accuracy and integrity of tax information, records and supporting documents. 2. Tax analysis and risk identification Review and analyse tax-related data, transactions, supporting documents and reconciliations to identify discrepancies, documentation gaps or tax risk indicators. Prepare tax analysis and supporting information to assist with the review of tax treatments, tax positions and compliance matters within the role’s scope. 3. Tax audit, tax health check and advisor coordination Coordinate information and documentation to support tax audits, tax health checks, regulatory reviews and information requests from external auditors, external tax advisors and relevant authorities. Prepare and maintain tax audit files, reconciliations, supporting evidence, schedules and working papers for assigned tax areas. 4. Tax technology, data quality and process improvement Support tax technology-enabled improvement initiatives, including tax data quality review, compliance trackers, documentation repositories, dashboards, templates and other tools that support tax compliance and audit readiness Use available finance systems, spreadsheets, data tools and templates to support tax data preparation, reconciliation, mapping, exception review and identification of tax risk indicators Work with relevant Finance, systems and process stakeholders to identify practical opportunities to streamline tax compliance activities, reduce manual work, improve tax data visibility and strengthen controls over tax related information. Contribute to the improvement of tax processes, checklists, templates, guidance notes and internal controls to enhance efficiency, compliance, documentation quality and audit readiness. 5. Stakeholder engagement Coordinate with Finance teams, internal stakeholders and external advisors on tax-related matters, information requests, documentation requirements and agreed follow-up actions. Support the implementation of tax guidance, process updates, risk mitigation actions and compliance improvements across relevant Finance and business processes. Key Selection Criteria Demonstrated 5–8 years' relevant experience in tax and/or accounting within a complex organisation, preferably in an international, education, not-for-profit, foreign direct investment (FDI), or multinational environment. Bachelor’s degree in accounting, Finance, Commerce, Taxation, or a related discipline. Professional accounting or tax qualifications (e.g., CPA, CA, ACCA, CTA) are advantageous. Sound working knowledge of Vietnamese tax regulations, financial reporting and compliance requirements, including VAT, FCT, CIT, PIT, tax administration, invoice requirements and supporting documentation principles. Experience preparing, reviewing or coordinating tax calculations, tax returns, reconciliations, supporting schedules, working papers and tax documentation. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to review financial and tax information, identify discrepancies or risk indicators and support practical issue resolution. Experience using financial systems, spreadsheets, tax data, reporting templates, dashboards or data visualisation tools to support tax reporting, reconciliation, analysis and compliance activities. Well-developed organizational and time management skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines and deliver accurate work with appropriate attention to detail. Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to work collaboratively with Finance teams, internal stakeholders and external advisors on tax-related matters. Ability to contribute to tax process improvement, data quality review, reporting automation, documentation management and system-enabled compliance initiatives. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. Read more details at Job Description HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 17 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Digital-Learning-Coordinator--Learning-Design--LMS-Administrator-_JR51186-1": {
      "title": "Digital Learning Coordinator, Learning Design (LMS Administrator)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full time, continuing position   HEW 7 ($107,747 - $116,630) + 17% Superannuation   Based at the Melbourne City campus plus hybrid and flexible working arrangements     About the Position   As the Digital Learning Coordinator, Learning Design (LMS Administrator), you’ll play a key role in enhancing the digital learning experience across the College of Business and Law. Working closely with Learning Design, School Operations, Student Experience teams and IT Services, you will lead the administration, coordination and continuous improvement of the College's Learning Management System (Canvas), ensuring high-quality, student-centered learning experiences across multiple programs, cohorts and delivery modes.    This role is responsible for LMS administration, course readiness and governance, supporting successful teaching period go-lives, resolving complex LMS issues, and driving initiatives that improve student engagement, participation and success. You will also provide expert advice, training and guidance to stakeholders while contributing to process improvement, innovation and the adoption of new technologies.    To be successful in this position you'll have:   Demonstrated experience administering Learning Management Systems, preferably Canvas, including course rollovers, enrolments, permissions, integrations and course maintenance.  Proven experience designing, implementing and continuously improving digital learning and student engagement initiatives within a complex organisation.  Strong understanding of LMS governance, service delivery and operational processes, with the ability to manage competing priorities and resolve complex issues.  Highly developed stakeholder engagement and relationship management skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively across academic, professional and technical teams.  Excellent communication, training and influencing skills, with the ability to provide specialist advice and build capability in others.  Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, including the ability to use data and insights to inform decision-making and continuous improvement.  Demonstrated experience driving process improvement, service innovation and the implementation of new technologies and automation solutions.  Relevant tertiary qualifications and/or equivalent experience.      Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.     About the College of Business and Law   Read about the College in the Position Description linked below and visit the College of Business and Law webpage .  To Apply    Please submit your CV and cover letter addressing your interest and suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.     For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Medina via email medina.hubanic@rmit.edu.au .    Position Description    Please note, if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, position description links may not work on LinkedIn advertisements.        #LI-Hybrid  Applications Close: 18 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/VE-Teacher--Air-Conditioning-and-Refrigeration_JR50792": {
      "title": "VE Teacher, Air Conditioning and Refrigeration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Fixed-Term position for 12 months Salary teacher level T3.1 to T5 + 17% Superannuation   Based at the Melbourne CBD or Bundoora campuses however, but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University     We are looking for current or aspiring VE Air Conditioning Teachers who have relevant industry and vocational teaching qualifications, or who are working towards a Certificate IV in Training & Assessment, Cert III and IV in Air-conditioning and Refrigeration, and Full Refrigeration and Air Conditioning Licence.    Great benefits such as 17% Superannuation, 720 teaching hours per year, 4 weeks leave plus 2 weeks VE leave     About the role     As a VE Teacher at RMIT, you will be mainly responsible for delivering course material, assessing students, and supervising students enrolled in selected courses in the schools.   Effective interpersonal and communication skills relevant to teaching and consultancy environments. This includes effective presentation and facilitation skills, and in the use of flexible teaching methods.   Skills and experience in competency-based assessment and ensuring current and contemporary vocational competence meets and/or exceeds the education level being delivered and assessed.   Experience in relevant industry, and substantial discipline knowledge as it relates to this position.   The capacity to diagnose learning problems in students and propose and implement effective solutions.     Qualifications   Certificate IV in Training & Assessment (TAE40110 as a minimum)   Certificate III and IV in Air-conditioning and Refrigeration  Full Refrigeration and Air Conditioning Licence     Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.     To Apply    Please submit your CV and cover letter addressing the Key selection criteria by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.  For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Mykayla via email at Mykayla.mccartin@rmit.edu.au        Position Description - VE Tacher, Air-conditioning and Refrigeration   If you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, position description links may not work on LinkedIn advertisements.      #LI-Hybrid  Applications Close: 31 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
